  "notes": "{六|ろく} is the number six. The native Japanese counting word is {六|むっ}つ (muttsu).\n\nSOUND CHANGES:\nWhen combined with counters starting with h-sounds, ろく often becomes ろっ:\n- {六|ろっ}{本|ぽん} (roppon): six long objects\n- {六|ろっ}{百|ぴゃく} (roppyaku): 600\n- {六|ろっ}{匹|ぴき} (roppiki): six animals\n\nNO CHANGE:\n- {六|ろく}{時|じ} (rokuji): six o'clock\n- {六|ろく}{人|にん} (rokunin): six people\n- ⟦{六|ろく}{月|がつ}→ろくがつ：00662⟧ (rokugatsu): June\n\nCULTURAL NOTE:\nSix is generally considered a lucky number in Japan.",
